--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyleft and reciprocal licences, stated explicitly
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@resvg/resvg-js (MPL-2.0), and its platform binary @resvg/resvg-js-*
    Used unmodified, as a published npm dependency of apps/api. No file covered
    by the MPL has been changed. Source: https://github.com/yisibl/resvg-js

web-push (MPL-2.0)
    Used unmodified, as a published npm dependency of apps/api. No file covered
    by the MPL has been changed.
    Source: https://github.com/web-push-libs/web-push

eslint-config-turbo, eslint-plugin-turbo (MPL-2.0)
    Development-only lint packages, used unmodified. Not present in any shipped
    image. Source: https://github.com/vercel/turbo

dompurify (dual MPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0)
    Apache-2.0 is elected. Used unmodified, as a dependency of apps/web.
    Source: https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify

jszip (dual MIT or GPL-3.0-or-later)
    MIT is elected. Used unmodified, as a transitive dependency.
    Source: https://github.com/Stuk/jszip

libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
    Not a source dependency of this repository. It is loaded dynamically by the
    `sharp` image library (Apache-2.0), which ships it as the prebuilt
    `@img/sharp-libvips-*` package, and it is therefore present in the Docker
    images built from `deploy/Dockerfile`. It is used unmodified and is linked
    dynamically, so it may be replaced with another build of libvips.
    Source: https://github.com/libvips/libvips

world-countries (ODbL-1.0)
    Reference data (country names, codes, currencies), used unmodified as data.
    Source: https://github.com/mledoze/countries

